&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 10pt; page-break-before: always; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 18pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;"&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 10pt; text-indent: -18pt;"&gt;(i)&lt;font style="width: 9.12pt; text-indent: 0pt; display: inline-block;"&gt; &amp;#160;&lt;/font&gt;On December&amp;#160;31, 2023, NYISO entered into a $100.0&amp;#160;million Revolving Term Loan Credit Facility (2024&amp;#8209;2028 Budget Facility) with an effective date of January&amp;#160;1, 2024 through December&amp;#160;31, 2028. The proceeds from this Term Loan Facility are to be used for capital purchases and significant projects during 2024 &amp;#8209;2028. Interest on borrowings under this Term Loan Facility is based on NYISO&amp;#8217;s option of varying rates of interest tied to either the prime rate or the SOFR plus 60 basis points. NYISO must convert each year&amp;#8217;s annual borrowings to term loans, with the principal and interest payments payable over three years.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 10pt;"&gt;The 2024&amp;#8209;2028 Budget Facility allows for a maximum of $100.0&amp;#160;million to be outstanding at any time. Under the revolving structure, loan amortization in proceeding years restores funds availability.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p style="margin-top: 0pt; margin-left: 36pt; margin-bottom: 10pt; page-break-after: avoid;"&gt;As of March 31, 2026 and 2025, the loan details on the 2024-2028 Budget Facility consists of the following:&lt;/p&gt;
